cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Does it transfer? A pluripotency-domain benchmark of temporal trajectory-inference methods across iPSC reprogramming systems, with scANVI-validated cell-state references"
version: v1.0.0-rc1
authors:
  - family-names: Kuma
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Frontier Sciences, The University of Tokyo"
    email: morri0723@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO
date-released: "2026-06-12"
license: MIT
keywords: [single-cell, trajectory inference, benchmarking, scANVI, scArches, reference mapping, out-of-distribution, induced pluripotency, reprogramming, reproducibility]
abstract: >
  Code, manuscript, and reproducibility materials for a single-domain
  (induced-pluripotency) benchmark of temporal single-cell trajectory-inference
  methods, built on the scTimeBench three-task design (forecast accuracy, embedding
  coherence, lineage fidelity). Contributes a reference-construction-and-validation
  pipeline in which silver cell-state references are built by scANVI/scArches label
  transfer and screened by a geometric out-of-distribution gate integrated into the
  main pipeline, and an analysis showing that lineage method rankings do not transfer
  across reprogramming systems and that single-seed leaderboards are unstable. Framed
  as a silver-reference benchmark and cautionary analysis rather than biological
  ground truth.
